Refuse a defective vocabulary with an error and keep the C API free of aborts
Fold-into: upstream/vocab

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- Two equal token texts stop the load with an assert.

  Two equal texts in tokenizer.ggml.tokens stop the load with GGML_ASSERT(id_to_token.size() == token_to_id.size()).

  The change: The load throws an error with the count of tokens and the count of different token texts, and
  llama_model_load_from_file returns NULL.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--vocab-dup-tokens.

- A BYTE token that the vocabulary cannot decode stops the load.

  A token of type BYTE in a WPM vocabulary, or a BYTE token with a text of fewer than 5 bytes,
  stops the load in token_to_byte with GGML_ABORT.

  The change: token_to_byte decodes a BYTE token only when its text is <0xHH>, for the SPM, UGM, BPE and WPM
  vocabularies. Each other BYTE token gives the byte '?', and the load continues.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--vocab-byte-type.

- The token functions of the C API abort for a vocabulary of type NONE.

  A vocab-only model with tokenizer.ggml.model = no_vocab loads, and then llama_vocab_get_text and
  the other token functions of the C API stop on GGML_ASSERT(type != LLAMA_VOCAB_TYPE_NONE).

  The change: The C functions give neutral values for such a vocabulary: an empty text, 0, no tokens.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--vocab-none-assert.

- An exception of the tokenizer leaves llama_tokenize.

  An SPM vocabulary without the byte tokens <0x00> to <0xFF> loads, and then byte_to_token throws
  std::out_of_range through llama_tokenize. An exception out of a C function stops the caller in
  std::terminate.

  The change: llama_tokenize catches the exception, writes an error line and returns INT32_MIN.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--spm-byte-tokens.

- The UTF-8 decoder accepts a 4-byte sequence above U+10FFFF.

  unicode_cpt_from_utf8 accepts a lead byte F4 with 90..BF and F5..F7, which give a value above
  U+10FFFF. unicode_cpt_to_utf8 then throws std::invalid_argument outside of each handler, and the
  exception leaves llama_tokenize.

  The change: The decoder refuses such a value, and unicode_cpts_from_utf8 replaces it with U+FFFD, as for each other invalid sequence.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_tokenizer--tokenizer-codepoint.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

